     "subtopic_code": "(k) Plasma Science and Technology—High Energy Density Physics",
     "subtopic_code_norm": "kpsathedp",
     "subtopic_id": "360678:kpsathedp",
     "subtopic_ordinal": 43,
     "subtopic_source": "inferred",
     "summary": "The High Energy Density Physics (HEDP) program seeks to understand how matter behaves under extreme conditions of temperature and pressure. In this domain, energy density is typically defined as being above 1 Mbar (100 GPa or approximately 1 million atmospheres), which is comparable to the energy density of a chemical bond, such as in a water molecule. HEDP conditions are crucial for studying processes such as the formation and destruction of stars and for controlling thermonuclear fusion in laboratory settings.",
