     "subtopic_code": "(l) Plasma Science and Technology—Microelectronics Research",
     "subtopic_code_norm": "lpsatmr",
     "subtopic_id": "360678:lpsatmr",
     "subtopic_ordinal": 44,
     "subtopic_source": "inferred",
     "summary": "Plasmas are essential to the manufacture of devices in the semiconductor industry, from the creation of extreme ultraviolet photons used in the most advanced lithography to thin film etching, deposition, and surface modifications. It is estimated that 40-45% of all process steps needed to manufacture semiconductor devices use low temperature plasmas (LTPs) in one form or another. LTPs have been an enabling technology in the multi-decade progression of the shrinking of device dimensions, often referred to as Moore’s Law.",
