     "subtopic_ordinal": 54,
     "subtopic_source": "inferred",
     "summary": "Quantum information science (QIS) is the study of how the unique behaviors of the microscopic world described by quantum mechanics – such as entanglement, superposition, and interference – can be used to solve scientific problems and build new technologies, such as quantum sensors and computers. HEP-QIS pursues the potential for QIS to solve previously intractable problems, measure previously undetectable signals, and bring new theoretical tools to bear on our understanding of the universe through our Quantum Information Science Enabled Discovery (QuantISED) program.",
